# Root .gitignore — universal rules + the Go services (the majority language).
# The Java service (bridge/) and the web app (web/) keep their own .gitignore
# for their toolchains. Line-ending rules live in .gitattributes.
#
# Patterns have no leading slash, so they match at ANY depth -- one entry here
# covers every nested service (e.g. `.env` catches api/.env, web/.env, ...).

# --- Secrets ---
.env
*.local.yml
application-local.yml

# --- Go build output (all Go services) ---
bin/
*.exe
*.test
*.out
vendor/

# --- Data / CUI: the LADD Industry file is CUI; never commit anything here ---
data/

# --- Editors ---
.vscode/
.idea/
*.iml

# --- OS ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Logs / scratch ---
*.log
logs/
captured/
private-drafts/
/deploy